 "07129d8d-82e3-5b90-a321-b803049449ab" :question/math-academy-id "q-10435" :question/problem "Find the asymptotes of the hyperbola ${y}^{2}-9{x}^{2}=9.$" :question/worked-solution "The standard equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at the origin is\n\n$$\n\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nFor a vertical hyperbola centered at the origin, the equations of the asymptotes are\n\n$$\ny=\\pm \\frac{a}{b}x.\n$$\n\nTo rewrite the given equation in standard form, we divide both sides of the equation by $9$ and then simplify, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2}-9{x}^{2} & =9 \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}-\\frac{9{x}^{2}}{9} & =\\frac{9}{9} \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{1} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have $a=\\sqrt{9}=3$ and $b=\\sqrt{1}=1.$\n\nTherefore, the asymptotes of the hyperbola are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\pm \\frac{3}{1}x \\\\  & =\\pm 3x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-10435/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ca7c76e6-204b-5b30-8e62-c53027b63448"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-10435"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-84082/selection/5aab90ab96afb4324401d8e74ee1bfa6616cc05f32fed7817a2edea6b1a3327b" :answer/id #uuid "9e3f6e7e-268f-5d10-913d-0c85e00f2d42" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\pm 8x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84082/selection/456331d6bb324a86c6366cc6322928c90711ff2a82e9426366dd2cb9ceda61dc" :answer/id #uuid "186ee738-7783-5bfd-b906-f39f2687548c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\pm \\frac{1}{2}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84082/selection/b31cecd316b6911ea5bd89055bbcc24f3ec86cd0a194a857d1c1b4737b8bb606" :answer/id #uuid "724204bd-f49d-5c09-bf7d-9ab9a309d295" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\pm 4x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84082/selection/14eccf8a242f0d8f0178f9b363c4d696262f7524f235d